    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9e69cba312c0355fdc732f58dd197249e30ce14ecb0d4d958d15c2a17097657a",
      "text": "Day 7 · Breakfast. Morning excursion to Tierra del Fuego National Park, with lunch and drinks in a large dining tent in the panoramic Cormorant Archipelago area. After a 25- to 40-minute drive, reach Ensenada Zaratiegui, home of the post office at the end of the world, for a short circular walk along the beach and through the forest, with views of Isla Redonda and the Chilean coast across the Beagle Channel. Continue to Lapataia Bay, where National Route 3 ends, the Lapataia and Ovando rivers, Laguna Verde and Lake Acigami (formerly Lake Roca).\n\nAfternoon · Navigation on the Beagle Channel to the Isla de los Pájaros, home to skuas, black-browed albatrosses, steamer ducks, kelp geese and gulls; the Isla de los Lobos, with South American sea lions and fur seals; and the Les Eclaireurs Lighthouse, often mistaken for the “Lighthouse at the End of the World”, with colonies of imperial and rock cormorants. Your guide explains the wildlife, the geography and the historic importance of the channel for the birth of the city.",
